      "interpretation": "The native raw First/Break indexes are integer-converted and indexed directly without a local bounds guard; First tag/time and Break main time come from raw market candles, while mode and box geometry come from public reaction. Confirmation uses raw reaction and default intrabar-start. Only previous First timestamp is protected by explicit 0 <= index < full main length. Reset display and second time are formatted from recorded fields with null defaults; this does not independently prove reset crossing.",
